# Traffic stop: Keitaro vs traffic source

**Keitaro is tracking + routing only.** Pausing a Keitaro campaign does **not** stop DSP/affiliate spend. Do not pause Keitaro campaigns to “stop traffic” or fix a down monetization feed.

## What to do instead

| Situation | Action |
|-----------|--------|
| Brand/multi-feed campaign, **more than one feed** attached and able to take traffic | In Keitaro: set the bad feed’s **share/weight to 0**, renormalize remaining feeds |
| Brand campaign with **only one live feed** (others at 0 or absent), or feed-specific child (e.g. NIPUHIM-adexa / BLEND-adexa) | **Pause the traffic source** campaign(s) that send into that Keitaro alias (SK / ZP / EC / …), not Keitaro |
| Unsure which source buys | Match SK (etc.) `trackingUrl` to the Keitaro campaign **alias**; pause those active source campaigns |

## Anti-pattern (2026-08-26 Adexa outage)

- Wrong: disabled Quality brand campaigns in Keitaro (`state=disabled`) while Adexa was down.
- Corrected: reactivated Keitaro; paused SourceKnowledge campaigns whose tracking URL used those aliases.

## Checklist before any “pause”

1. Goal is stop **spend**? → traffic source API (`active: false` / equivalent).
2. Goal is stop sending to **one affiliation** but keep the brand live? → Keitaro flow **shares** only.
3. Confirm with dry-run which layer you will change; never default to Keitaro campaign disable.
